{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_0118704fd7b54b2bb9750adf","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 131 lines\n1: Completed-GMT: 2026-10-11 06:59:41 GMT\n2: Completed-Local: 2026-10-11 13:59:41 Asia/Bangkok\n3: \n4: # VM Engineer — semantic-register-vm phase 6, slice 6c-pre\n5: \n6: Implemented in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6cpre`, branch `srvm-phase6cpre`. No staging or commits. No design edits, semantic-register edits, register-kernel edits, or existing test edits. Sign-off remains with the designated non-author claude-fable-5-1 reviewer; this is an implementation report, not review sign-off.\n7: \n8: ## Changed files\n9: \n10: - Modified: `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc`. Tail `:call` effect park builders add `:resume-mode :return-result`. Restore completes the retained-FFI/response steps first, then routes marked entries through the same return transition as `:return`. That transition pops the innermost frame, truncates to its cumulative stack base, pushes the delivered value, restores caller pc/frames/store context, or halts with `[value]` and clears store context when K is empty.\n11: - New: `test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc` — 9 tests / 25 assertions on JVM and Node.\n12: - New: this report. Supporting command scripts, logs, mutation driver and verified backups are under `collab/6cpre-*`; they are evidence artifacts and remain unstaged.\n13: \n14: The marker is added only by effect park builders for a tail `:call`; ordinary instruction parks, captured continuations, non-tail calls, and synchronous call results retain their existing paths.\n15: \n16: ## Exact lane outcomes\n17: \n18: | Lane | Outcome | Counts and evidence |\n19: |---|---|---|\n20: | G0 JVM, new namespace | PASS after fixture correction | 9 tests, 25 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; `6cpre-g0.log` |\n21: | JVM selected regression group, final source | PASS, exit 0 | 78 namespaces, 1,345 tests,