estores-caller-environment` check inner-frame removal, retained outer frame, exact residual stack plus nil value, return pc, caller lexical frames and module store context. `tail-in-operand-position-skips-layout` also exercises a real closure caller and scheduler wake.\n54: 3. **PASS — empty K halts with the result.** `empty-k-halts-with-result` wakes an actual root tail effect with nil, checks halt/value/stack/store context, and cannot accidentally treat nil as missing delivery.\n55: 4. **PASS — tail call in operand position skips following layout syntax.** `tail-in-operand-position-skips-layout` parks at pc 10 with a saved outer operand, then returns 7 directly with stack `[:outer 7]`; following push/100/enclosing addition do not execute.\n56: 5. **PASS — retained FFI and response decoding stay before delivery (§4.3).** `retained-ffi-reparks-before-return` checks reader re-park, blocked state, preserved marker/K and removal of the writer marker; `ffi-response-decodes-before-return` checks decoded nil delivery and parked-call cleanup. These are constructed native-entry seam tests, not a claim that a new tail-FFI opcode was added.\n57: 6. **PASS — non-tail parks and old stack tests unchanged.** Final JVM selected regression group and broad Node group pass; `non-tail-park-keeps-successor` returns the old successor result `:layout` with stack `[:result :layout]`. `git diff --quiet HEAD --` checks confirm unchanged existing stack tests, semantic-register files and register kernel.\n58: 7. **PASS on JVM/Node; Dart NOT RUN — verification.** Exact lane results above. Source lint/style/whitespace checks pass. Tri-host verification remains incomplete until the orchestrator runs Dart.\n59: \n60: ## Tests that can fail: temporary source mutations\n61: \n62: Before each mutation pass, copied the implemented source byte for byte to `collab/6cpre-stack-implemented.backup.cljc` and verified it with `cmp`. Also saved the original HEAD source to `collab/6cpre-stack-head.backup.cljc